    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Is it possible to add a figure to a mirt figure? For example, suposse tha one wansts to plot some points of interest over the figure produced by the function &quot;itemplot(result,1,type=&quot;trace&quot;)&quot;. Howe could one do that?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot,</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Caio</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "o2GkrbnoAAAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2017-09-14T14:44:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: Adding plots/lines to existing plots",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This requires the use of the latticeExtra package for the most part. Because all of mirt&#39;s plots are generated based on lattice (which allows post-editing them easier as well) then you&#39;ll need to use tricks related to this graphical system. E.g., <a href=\"http://latticeextra.r-forge.r-project.org/man/layer.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://latticeextra.r-forge.r-project.org/man/layer.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474242282000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ozkxP290rx57KiNBBJPxP\">http://latticeextra.r-forge.r-project.org/man/layer.html</a></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
